---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';

const subscriptionsEnabled = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SUBSCRIPTIONS_ENABLED === 'true';

// TODO before launch: add the operating legal entity, its registered address and,
// if required in your jurisdiction, a data protection contact. Have a lawyer review.
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy notice — KAVOVO"
  description="What data KAVOVO collects, why, and how to have it removed."
>
  <TextPage
    eyebrow="Privacy"
    title="Privacy notice"
    intro="A short, honest description of what happens to data when you visit KAVOVO."
    updated="2026-08-21"
  >
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      KAVOVO is a static website. We do not run advertising, we do not set tracking cookies, and we do not sell or share
      personal data. We use limited cookieless analytics to understand how selected site features work in aggregate. {
        subscriptionsEnabled
          ? 'We collect an email address only when you choose to subscribe to the newsletter or shop waitlist.'
          : 'Newsletter and waitlist sign-ups are currently disabled, so the site does not accept email addresses.'
      }
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>No account or tracking cookie.</strong> Reading recipes, guides, lessons and Journal articles requires no
        account and sets no cookies from us.
      </li>
      {
        subscriptionsEnabled && (
          <li>
            <strong>Your email address and sign-up source,</strong> if you submit the newsletter or shop waitlist form.
            Brevo also records the sign-up and confirmation dates so we can send the right emails and demonstrate
            consent.
          </li>
        )
      }
      <li>
        <strong>Limited product events,</strong> described below. These contain predefined categories, content slugs and
        settings, not your recipe values or free text.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Progress and recipe preferences on your device.</strong> Completed lesson slugs, saved and recently
        viewed recipe slugs, timestamps and your unit preference stay in your browser storage. They are not synced to
        KAVOVO or between devices.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Local browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      Learn progress, saved recipes, recently viewed recipes and recipe unit preferences use versioned local storage.
      These features store only content slugs, timestamps and settings. You can remove individual saved recipes, clear
      recent history, reset one learning path, or clear the site data through your browser. If storage is blocked, the
      main site still works and these controls fall back to the current page session where possible.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical request data — including IP
      address, browser type and requested URL — to deliver pages and protect against abuse. We do not use that data to
      build profiles of visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      We use PostHog, hosted in the EU, for limited cookieless product analytics. It tells us which parts of the Brew
      Assistant, learning paths and recipe tools people use, without telling us who they are.
    </p>
    <p>
      PostHog is configured with cookies, autocapture, pageview capture, person profiles and session recording all off.
      Events are sent only at the specific points we have chosen.
    </p>
    <p>Depending on the event, the properties sent are:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>entry point, whether a returning brew exists, and espresso or filter method group;</li>
      <li>the selected method and a predefined issue category;</li>
      <li>rule ID, adjustment type, direction and attempt number;</li>
      <li>whether feedback was helpful;</li>
      <li>related-content type and canonical content slug;</li>
      <li>learning path, lesson and recipe slugs for explicit completion, save and navigation actions;</li>
      <li>the selected servings multiplier or unit system, but never the entered espresso dose;</li>
      <li>validation step and predefined error category;</li>
      <li>the analytics schema version attached to every event.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do not send your email address, free text, exact dose, yield, water, brew time or temperature, a full recipe,
      or any session ID. Brew history, Learn progress, Saved recipes and Recently viewed history stay in your own
      browser and are never uploaded.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you block analytics with a browser extension or a content blocker, the Brew Assistant carries on working
      exactly as before.
    </p>

    <h2>Newsletter</h2>
    {
      subscriptionsEnabled ? (
        <>
          <p>
            Newsletter and shop waitlist subscriptions use Brevo as our email processor. When you submit a form, Brevo
            sends a double opt-in message. You are added to the selected list only after following its confirmation link.
            The sign-up source is stored so we send only the updates you requested.
          </p>
          <p>
            We keep a confirmed address while the subscription is active. If you unsubscribe or ask for deletion, we
            remove it from active mailing lists; a minimal suppression record may remain so the opt-out continues to be
            honoured. Consent and delivery records are kept only as long as needed to demonstrate compliance and resolve
            delivery or legal issues. Every marketing email includes an unsubscribe link.
          </p>
          <p>
            Brevo processes this information on our behalf. Read the{' '}
            <a href="https://www.brevo.com/legal/privacypolicy/" rel="external">
              Brevo privacy policy
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p>
          Newsletter and shop waitlist forms are currently disabled. KAVOVO does not collect or send email addresses to
          an email provider while they remain disabled.
        </p>
      )
    }

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Unsubscribe at any time using the link in any email we send.</li>
      <li>
        Ask us what we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask for it to be deleted, by emailing
        <a href="mailto:hello@kavovo.uk">hello@kavovo.uk</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We aim to answer requests within 30 days.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      When this notice changes we update the date at the top. Material changes to how we handle email addresses will
      also be announced in the newsletter itself.
    </p>
  </TextPage>
</Layout>
